      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T10:25:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To speculate about the language (IANAL), I\u0027d say that the previous\n```\ndata.end \u003d\u003d bss.start\n```\nwas inlined as\n```\naddr_of!(data_end) \u003d\u003d addr_of!(bss_start)\n```\nwhich was a comparison between _place expressions_ (hence optimization through aliasing) while `end` is now forced to store the result of a _value expression_.\n\n\u003e I still think you should just have pointers to the various region start \u0026 end, populated by the linker/assembly. \n\nI\u0027m not sure how to give a _value_ to a C/Rust variable from the linker script (where variables are _addresses_) and how to tell the linker to write the size of `.rodata` in a variable in `.rodata`(?)",
      "parentUuid": "8adff98a_14bae191",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "9871b92a173c1a50340b0e450db25f9e51b4bd4e",
