      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T12:37:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe there is something in the language to prevent this but on the IR level the compiler needs to have two basic pinhole optimizations:\n```\n1) A + B - A \u003d B\n2) if (A \u003d X as uN) and (B \u003d Y as uN) then (A \u003d\u003d B \u003c\u003d\u003e X \u003d\u003d Y)\n```\n(the `checked_add` is probably playing a role here as well).\n\n\u003e I\u0027m not sure how to give a value to a C/Rust variable from the linker script (where variables are addresses) and how to tell the linker to write the size of .rodata in a variable in .rodata(?)\n\nYou can have a simple C file linked in that contains:\n```\nuintptr_t val_rodata_end \u003d (uintptr_t)\u0026rodata_end;\n...\n```\nThis will compile into a relocation populated by the linker.",
